{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774495727,"nonce":"1dT7m5Bz0rsB0OcLuh/T6mE+vXA=","title":"User action: /showme command to display source code of a class/function by name","message":"A user action (similar to a Claude skill) that lets users quickly inspect source code by name.\n\nUsage: /showme SimpleFeedbackState\nEffect: Finds and displays the full source code of the named class/function/module.\n\nShould search across all repos in the workspace, showing the file path and line numbers. Could also support:\n- /showme SimpleFeedbackState --context 20 (show 20 lines of surrounding context)\n- /showme feedbax.bodies.SimpleFeedbackState (fully qualified)\n- /showme --callers SimpleFeedbackState (show where it's used)\n\nThis is useful when the user wants to verify how something is implemented without navigating files manually.\n\nImplementation: Could be a Claude Code skill that uses grep/ast to find definitions, or a Mandible UI action that queries the codebase index.","files":null}]}